<title>USA: Columbia Bancorp sees Q3 $0.14 SAIF charge.</title>
<headline>Columbia Bancorp sees Q3 $0.14 SAIF charge.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Columbia Bancorp said Friday that its third quarter earnings would include a one-time charge, after-tax charge of about $300,000, or about $0.14 per share, to go toward recapitalization of the Savings Association Insurance Fund.</p>
<p>Based upon projected lower SAIF deposit insurance rates as a result of the SAIF recapitalization, Columbia Bancorp said its SAIF deposit premiums should decline, increasing annual net income about $85,000 after-tax.</p>
</text>
